From ab33f7ab4cbe74db96bf5652c51abc733e2ad400 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:13:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] WSFANOUT + TAKEOVER: web bridge -- tag patches computed
 once per baseline, 64 connections, control.takeover
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260926 on the machine: "遮 CW 極限 sensor，瀏覽器要等接近 3 秒才變". Measured: the 1203 Poll ran every ~200 ms
(78 ms each) and the page polled every 500 ms, but every HTTP request (even a static file) waited ~0.7 s for its first
byte, and one wb_serve thread sat at 100% of a core. Then, after a restart, the HMI froze completely.
- WebBridgeServer PumpSnapshot: it diffed ~6,400 tags and COPIED the whole tag map once PER WS CONNECTION on every snapshot
  generation (~5/s, the 1203 Poll republishes). Conn::lastSent is now a shared immutable map (std::shared_ptr); the patch is
  computed and encoded once per distinct baseline and the same frame goes to every connection on that baseline; `lastSent =
  cur` is O(1). Frames are byte-identical to before (each connection still gets the delta against what IT last received;
  a mid-run joiner has its own baseline).
- wb_serve: cfg.maxConnections 16 -> 64 (cap FD_SETSIZE 128 - 8 = 120). Measured 23 TCP connections (every HMI window opens
  1-2 WebSockets + the pages' HTTP polls): with the default 16 the rest sat in the listen backlog forever, so Motor Test's
  /api/struct/motor/runtime never got an answer.
- control.takeover (EastSun "我進入IO頁面就應該把控制權拿回來" / "我在哪一頁按按鈕，那一頁就把控制權拿回來"): answered on the socket
  thread like control.acquire, but moves the single-operator token to the caller whoever holds it (loopback-only bridge, one
  operator at the HMI); the old holder gets not-operator on its next command. control.acquire is unchanged. Web side (web
  commit): IO outputs, Motor Test / Teach motor buttons, START/PAUSE/lot start and every Save use takeover; automatic sends
  (formShow/formClose sync, editlist.get, keepAlive, dryRun preview) keep acquire. Root cause of the IO page lock-out at
  start-up: the hidden Motor Test iframe's formClose sync took the token at load and never gave it back.
Line counts unchanged in both files (same-line edits), so every :NNNN citation of them still points where it did.
Verified on the machine by EastSun: limit lamp now follows the sensor without the 3 s delay; IO outputs work right after
start-up; IO page -> Motor Test Servo Off works (was control-held). Build build_integ_ship_x86 exit 0; WB_/JsonBridge/Sjson/
WebMotorAccess/WebWindowRegistry/IoPoints/MotorPoints/IoWatch ctest subset 20/20; production_audit 0 changes; pe_truncation
178 complete.
Known edge (not changed): if Motor Test runs HOME/Loop and the IO page takes over, the IO page's 30 s release leaves no owner
and MotorAccessPollTick cancels Motor Test's jobs (no stop is sent; the running leg finishes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
